; Andree, Programming the IBM 650 (1958), Problem Set 3-11, problem 1(a):
; "Each of the following programs adds 0000000001's to the upper half of
; the accumulator from the drum. Put each on the drum and let it run for
; 1 minute. Examine the totals in the upper accumulator at the end of
; each run."  Compare with count_optimum.650.
;
; The AUP loops on itself. Its constant at 0202 has already passed the
; heads when it's ready for it, and once it has added, 0201 has gone by
; too: two revolutions per add.
;
; Try:  r, wait a minute, Enter, then p   (or: ibm650 --run --max-rev 12500)

start 0200

0200  RAU 0202 0201
0201  AUP 0202 0201

0202  1+                ; the constant
